From 44e4b09d9263e839a946009464cc312e2067449b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abdulaziz <alanziabdulaziz4@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 05:27:49 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 06/15] llama: per-sequence rollback snapshot budget
 (llama_memory_seq_rs_snapshots)

The recurrent memory widens its R/S tensors to (1 + n_rs_seq) planes and every
ubatch writes min(T, n_rs_seq + 1) of them for every sequence, whether or not
that sequence will ever roll back. Add a per-seq budget rs_n_snap in
[0, n_rs_seq], default n_rs_seq (every existing caller keeps today's behaviour),
settable through the new public API and forwarded by the hybrid memory:

  - llama_memory_recurrent::seq_rm accepts a partial tail removal only up to the
    seq's budget; a budget-0 seq refuses exactly like a memory with n_rs_seq == 0,
    so a caller sees the FULL-type behaviour for that sequence.
  - llama_memory_recurrent_context::get_n_snap() = max budget over the seqs of
    the ubatch apply() just placed (n_rs_seq for the reserve context so the
    compute buffers fit the largest graph, 0 without snapshots). Side-effect
    free, so it is valid at graph build and again in can_reuse.

Nothing resets the budget but the API (seq_rm / clear / state_read leave it),
and no graph consumes it yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QrdPnP5KL449GsoWBZx52R
